---
name: add-business-rule
description: Adds a business rule (a check that rejects an operation with a localized error, such as unique names or allowed state changes) to a feature of this nArchitecture project. Use when the user asks to validate against the database or enforce a domain rule.
---

# Add a business rule

Input validation (required, length, format) belongs in the request's FluentValidation validator. Use a business rule for
checks that need data or domain knowledge.

All paths are under `{{ root }}/Application/Features/<PluralEntity>/`.

1. Add the message key to `Constants/<PluralEntity>BusinessMessages.cs`:

   ```csharp
   public const string TodoItemTitleAlreadyExists = "TodoItemTitleAlreadyExists";
   ```

2. Add its text to every locale file in `Resources/Locales/` (`<PluralEntity>.en.yaml`, and the other languages
   if there are any):

   ```yaml
   TodoItemTitleAlreadyExists: A todo item with this title already exists.
   ```

3. Add the rule to `Rules/<Entity>BusinessRules.cs`. Rules are `async Task` methods named after what must be true, and
   fail through the class's `throwBusinessException`, which localizes the message:

   ```csharp
   public async Task TodoItemTitleShouldBeUnique(string title)
   {
       bool exists = await _todoItemRepository.AnyAsync(predicate: t => t.Title == title);
       if (exists)
           await throwBusinessException(TodoItemsBusinessMessages.TodoItemTitleAlreadyExists);
   }
   ```

4. Call it from the handlers that need it, before changing any data.

5. `dotnet build`, and add a test for the rule if the solution has tests for the feature.
